# ALL.moderef — CEO-581 PER-MODE REFS for the Icon master. One row per invocation-determined line:
#   entry<TAB>mode<TAB>ref-line<TAB>mode-line<TAB>receipt
# The ref-line is the line AS STORED IN ALL.ref (verbatim, leading spaces included); the mode-line is what
# the ORACLE prints for that mode's invocation. Nothing is hidden: the line is still graded in full, against
# the answer that invocation actually produces. ⛔ THE RECEIPT IS MANDATORY AND IT IS THE ORACLE RUN, NEVER A
# FAILING DIFF (CEO-581's guard): a seat that cuts a second ref because m4 disagreed and it did not know why
# has committed the defect this file exists to stop, and that is a FAIL not a ref. Default stays ONE ref; the
# pair names itself. ⛔ NO WILDCARD: a pair is earned by measuring ONE program under both invocations.
procedure_every_alt_replace_4	m4	   &progname: procedure_every_alt_replace_4.icn	   &progname: ./procedure_every_alt_replace_4	ORACLE-MEASURED hq_V 2026-09-11 18:09 CDT, Arizona Icon 9.5.25a (/home/resources/icon-master/bin/icont), on THIS ENTRY OWN SOURCE extracted from ALL.icn and run under BOTH invocations: "icon procedure_every_alt_replace_4.icn" answered "   &progname: procedure_every_alt_replace_4.icn" (byte-identical to the stored ref) and "icont -s procedure_every_alt_replace_4.icn" then "./procedure_every_alt_replace_4" answered "   &progname: ./procedure_every_alt_replace_4". &progname is argv[0] VERBATIM (FINDING-2026-09-11-hq_V-progname-is-argv-zero-verbatim-so-pinning-makes-it-gradable-and-cannot-make-it-equal.md), so mode 4 IS the program and can never print the .icn form, and mode 3 is handed a SOURCE and can never print the ./ form. Both answers are the oracle. CEO-581 option one.
